      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and no standard protocol that I know of uses amlodipine 50 mg daily. The dose is five times the labeled maximum, and an overdose could be serious and hard to reverse. Monitoring wouldn't offset that, because amlodipine's effects last a long time.\n\nThese options are open to you:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, and the dose can be titrated later.\n- **Use the protocol's own order set.** If the high-dose protocol is real, it should have an order set or a pharmacist-verified entry path. Ordering through that path keeps the verification on record.\n- **Get a second check.** Ask the pharmacist who reviewed it, or the attending, to enter or co-sign the order directly. Then the approval is visible in the system and not just stated in chat.\n\nIf you want one of the standard doses, tell me which and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
